      "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWhpbWUtbnAuY28uanAvYXJ0aWNsZS9uZXdzMjAyNjExMjcwMDA0",
      "headline": "【愛媛で１４年ぶり確認】知っておきたい「はしか」の基本と予防接種の有効性　愛媛県立衛生環境研究所・四宮博人所長が解説",
      "headlineTranslated": "Measles confirmed in Ehime for the first time in 14 years: The basics of measles and the effectiveness of vaccination you should know, explained by Director Hiroto Shinomiya of the Ehime Prefectural Institute of Public Health and Environmental Research.",
      "summary": "Three measles cases were confirmed in Ehime Prefecture as of November 26, 2026, the first in the region since 2012 (14 years). Nationwide, 582 cases had been recorded as of November 18, 2026, more than double the 265 cases in 2013. Dr. Hiroto Shinomiya, director of the Ehime Prefectural Institute of Public Health and Environmental Research, explains measles’ high contagion with about a 10-day incubation, initial fever, cough and runny nose, then fever above 39°C and rash after 2–3 days, and potential complications such as pneumonia and encephalitis, including death. There is no specific antiviral treatment; management is supportive. Vaccination is highlighted as protective, and Ehime Prefecture advises individuals with suspected measles to contact healthcare providers before visiting. The article delivers the basics of measles and vaccination effectiveness as public health guidance.",
      "summaryOriginal": "Three measles cases were confirmed in Ehime Prefecture as of November 26, 2026, the first in the region since 2012 (14 years). Nationwide, 582 cases had been recorded as of November 18, 2026, more than double the 265 cases in 2013. Dr. Hiroto Shinomiya, director of the Ehime Prefectural Institute of Public Health and Environmental Research, explains measles’ high contagion with about a 10-day incubation, initial fever, cough and runny nose, then fever above 39°C and rash after 2–3 days, and potential complications such as pneumonia and encephalitis, including death. There is no specific antiviral treatment; management is supportive. Vaccination is highlighted as protective, and Ehime Prefecture advises individuals with suspected measles to contact healthcare providers before visiting. The article delivers the basics of measles and vaccination effectiveness as public health guidance.",
